post_install() {
  cat <<'MSG'

castr is installed. Two things are worth knowing:

  1. Neither backend's dependencies are pulled in automatically.

     For an Apple TV:
       yay -S doubletake-git
     Version 0.4.0 cannot capture on Hyprland; the git package can.

     For a Chromecast:
       sudo pacman -S gst-plugin-pipewire gst-plugins-base gst-plugins-good \
                      gst-plugins-bad gst-libav gst-plugin-va

  2. Your firewall must let the receiver reach this machine. Both backends
     need mDNS; the ports differ because the receivers connect differently.

       sudo ufw allow 5353/udp                 # discovery, both

     An Apple TV connects back into:
       sudo ufw allow 60000:60010/tcp
       sudo ufw allow 60000:60010/udp

     A Chromecast fetches the stream FROM this machine, so it needs the one
     port castr serves on -- and only from your own network:
       sudo ufw allow from 192.168.0.0/16 to any port 8010 proto tcp

Then run `castr menu`, or bind it to a key. The bar indicator lives in
/usr/share/castr/ -- Quickshell for Omarchy Quarto and later, waybar for
earlier setups.

MSG
}

post_upgrade() {
  # Settings and hand-added receivers are copied from omarchy-cast on first
  # run, if it was installed. It is left untouched and keeps working.
  :
}
